{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388123-help-me-understand-discarding-instruments-in-m20","id":1388123,"title":"Help me understand discarding instruments in M20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-13T12:51:27-07:00","id":1388123,"title":"Help me understand discarding instruments in M20","content":"This system just seems so... wrong to me. It says that you have to pick a minimum of 7 instruments or more. So far so good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then it says that you discard one instrument per Arete over 2. So if you have 7 or 8 instruments i guess it's workable. Some paradigms would really not need more than that and there's nothing wrong with this. But then there are the paradigms for which you would need at least twice that number even if you made the most generic by the book character possible with a very &quot;standard&quot; paradigm.<br /> So you are left with needing a ridiculous number of instruments even when you have run out Arete... i realize this issue is mostly theoretical (i mean how often do you get Atete 9-10 mages after all)<br /> but it still presents you with a very annoying problem.<br /> <br /> Namely the fact that your paradigm does not necessarily use all of these instruments for each and every one of these spheres! At least according to every tradition/convention/craft book that has ever been written. Indeed some can be wildly different.<br /> <br /> So you are left with moderately high Arete Akashics, for instance, needing literally no instruments for many of their spheres, not because their players are cheating, but because this is literally how their paradigm may work. They are just not that heavy on using an extremely diverge number of foci.(but if i am wrong, the same can apply to another group. I just used the akashics for the sake of convenience)<br /> <br /> <br /> At least compared to,say, the wu lung who,even if you house rule that at Arete 9 you need no instruments no matter what, would be forced to use a wide plethora of instruments until they reach this nigh-mythical rating<br /> <br /> I am not sure if that was intentional or just an oversight<br /> <br /> I personally think that second edition's system was much more clean cut<br /> I would appreciate to know what everyone things on the matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:08:45-07:00","id":1388128,"title":"","content":"This is something that really comes down to the nature of how mages steadily awaken.<br /> <br /> They require low arete because they need support as they experiment with radically altering reality to fit their paradigm. Even a relatively low instrument paradigm aesthetically such as an Ecstatic or Akashyana, the instrument lists actually provide plenty of options. A tradition Akashyana might use meditation, focus, kata, martial arts, mantra, breathing, staffs, or self-cleansing; some of them may be a lot easier to implement then a Hermetic or Progenitor, but that's the nature of their paradigms and it's the balance of pros and cons in setting.<br /> <br /> However as Willworkers develop, they become more confident and certain. They don't necessarily need some of their training Wills as they tie themselves intrinsically into their mystic paradigm. The living Saint doesn't necessarily need to take the time and go through the rosary exactly like he did as an acolyte; his prayer is enough.<br /> <br /> You also aren't entirely abandoning your instruments, you even gain bonuses to casting by using instruments you no longer technically need and you will still require your general instruments. If my Virtual Adept has outgrown her need to use caffeine pills and adderall to heighten her focus, she can comprehend the web just fine with her suped up rig, but sometimes she pops pills for an extra bit of oomph. Nothing wrong with that, but she's more confident then she was as a wee bab script kiddie.<br /> <br /> Plus, the path to Ascension is the innate realization that everything has been training wheels on the road to fulfilling the potential you always had and then simply doing it.<br /> <br /> But Mage is a game of perspectives, this is just mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:23:50-07:00","id":1388133,"title":"","content":"This sort of thing is the reason why I implemented the house rule I use for discarding instruments: instead of discarding them one at a time as your Arete increases, you discard them <i>all at once</i> \u2014 but only if you're working a sufficiently low-level Effect. <br /> <br /> At Arete 2 (Arete 6 for technomancers), you no longer need Instruments for level 1 Effects.<br /> <br /> At Arete 4 (Arete 7 for technomancers), you no longer need Instruments for level 2 Effects.<br /> <br /> At Arete 6 (Arete 8 for technomancers), you no longer need Instruments for level 3 Effects.<br /> <br /> At Arete 8 (Arete 9 for technomancers), you no longer need Instruments for level 4 Effects.<br /> <br /> At Arete 10 (except for Technocrats), you no longer need Instruments. <br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if you have 7 Instruments, 20 Instruments, or (theoretically) 3 Instruments; if your Arete exceeds the rank of the Effect you're attempting by enough (double the rank for mystics; five dots more than the rank for technomancers), you don't need to use any of them. <br /> <br /> This means that you get to choose what Instruments you use without having to worry about how that will affect the \u201cdropping Instruments\u201d system: whether you want everything channeled through a single Instrument or you want a different Instrument for each Effect that you perform \u2014 or even for each time you perform an Effect, just to go to an utterly ridiculous extreme \u2014 it works just as well. It also means that you don't need to throw in caveats like \u201cthe Instrument that you use the most is the one that you discard last\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-13-2020, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:25:41-07:00","id":1388135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388123-help-me-understand-discarding-instruments-in-m20?p=1388128#post1388128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that really comes down to the nature of how mages steadily awaken.<br /> <br /> They require low arete because they need support as they experiment with radically altering reality to fit their paradigm. Even a relatively low instrument paradigm aesthetically such as an Ecstatic or Akashyana, the instrument lists actually provide plenty of options. A tradition Akashyana might use meditation, focus, kata, martial arts, mantra, breathing, staffs, or self-cleansing; some of them may be a lot easier to implement then a Hermetic or Progenitor, but that's the nature of their paradigms and it's the balance of pros and cons in setting.<br /> <br /> However as Willworkers develop, they become more confident and certain. They don't necessarily need some of their training Wills as they tie themselves intrinsically into their mystic paradigm. The living Saint doesn't necessarily need to take the time and go through the rosary exactly like he did as an acolyte; his prayer is enough.<br /> <br /> You also aren't entirely abandoning your instruments, you even gain bonuses to casting by using instruments you no longer technically need and you will still require your general instruments. If my Virtual Adept has outgrown her need to use caffeine pills and adderall to heighten her focus, she can comprehend the web just fine with her suped up rig, but sometimes she pops pills for an extra bit of oomph. Nothing wrong with that, but she's more confident then she was as a wee bab script kiddie.<br /> <br /> Plus, the path to Ascension is the innate realization that everything has been training wheels on the road to fulfilling the potential you always had and then simply doing it.<br /> <br /> But Mage is a game of perspectives, this is just mine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am well aware of the in-game justification for no longer needing instruments. I just mentioned only the out of game aspects for the sake of convenience<br /> My issue is not that it's bad that Akashics use fewer instrument. That's absolutely fine. Literally nothing wrong with it.<br /> <br /> My issue is that as written a moderately high arete akashic will not need to use instruments for many of his spheres..because it's not as if all 7-9 of his instruments are suitable for all the spheres. Maybe he needs only 2-3 for most(though not necessarily all) his mind effects for instance<br /> <br /> But the Hermetic/verbena/wu lung will always need so many instruments for every single sphere that discarding one instrument is a joke. Might as well not do it. At least according to literally every single book written since 1993. I could pick any of them blindly and point to an example.<br /> And again you are left with the problem of Arete caping at 10... am i the only one who sees an issue with an Arete 8-10 guy still needing 11+ instruments?<br /> That's why second edition's system was much better in my opinion. Or Revised. Or sorcerer crusade.. or Dark ages Mage or even first edition<br /> <br /> <br /> As it stand i am left with the option of either playing an actual Hermetic/verbena/Batini/Wulung/etc... or playing the Harry Potter version of him. A wand, a voice, a cauldron, some ingredients,,maybe looking at the stars..aka NOT how these real life occult systems would work<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A far better system would say&quot; At arete 3 and for each point thereafter you discard 1/7 of your instruments rounded up or down if you are a mystic. If you are a technomancer you do the same at Arete 6. Then 2/7 at Arete 7 and so on.<br /> Still more complicated than the previous systems, but i could see such a modified system working very nicely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 05-13-2020, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:31:40-07:00","id":1388137,"title":"","content":"M20 confusing? You don't say......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:33:57-07:00","id":1388140,"title":"","content":"Well digging into what seem to be some of your core issues and answering them from my perspective...<br /> <br /> First of all, I don't necessarily agree that any one Mage will necessarily be required to do just a few things to do their work, paradigms are broad and flexible and mages can have plenty of fun coming up with clever work arounds to use their paradigm and focus to fit certain issues.<br /> <br /> As well, until a Mage is ascending, they aren't necessarily relying upon each of their instruments, the ones that have become less necessary are simply that: less necessary. They are still useful and from a mechanical perspective you get a bonus for using instruments you don't necessarily need to and I think that's plenty of incentive to hold onto artifacts.<br /> <br /> Plus at these high levels of arete the mages have become so closely bound to their paradigm that it is more and more an expression of their Will with the instruments as something of a formality.<br /> <br /> I don't have any problem with someone preferring the older systems, naturally go for it, but I think the current system expresses what it means to rather well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:37:58-07:00","id":1388143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388123-help-me-understand-discarding-instruments-in-m20?p=1388133#post1388133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sort of thing is the reason why I implemented the house rule I use for discarding instruments: instead of discarding them one at a time as your Arete increases, you discard them <i>all at once</i> \u2014 but only if you're working a sufficiently low-level Effect.<br /> <br /> At Arete 2 (Arete 6 for technomancers), you no longer need Instruments for level 1 Effects.<br /> <br /> At Arete 4 (Arete 7 for technomancers), you no longer need Instruments for level 2 Effects.<br /> <br /> At Arete 6 (Arete 8 for technomancers), you no longer need Instruments for level 3 Effects.<br /> <br /> At Arete 8 (Arete 9 for technomancers), you no longer need Instruments for level 4 Effects.<br /> <br /> At Arete 10 (except for Technocrats), you no longer need Instruments.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if you have 7 Instruments, 20 Instruments, or (theoretically) 3 Instruments; if your Arete exceeds the rank of the Effect you're attempting by enough (double the rank for mystics; five dots more than the rank for technomancers), you don't need to use any of them.<br /> <br /> This means that you get to choose what Instruments you use without concern<br /> having to worry about how that will affect the \u201cdropping Instruments\u201d system: whether you want everything channeled through a single Instrument or you want a different Instrument for each Effect that you perform \u2014 or even for each time you perform an Effect, just to go to an utterly ridiculous extreme \u2014 it works just as well. It also means that you don't need to throw in caveats like \u201cthe Instrument that you use the most is the one that you discard last\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually LOVE your system.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think may be even better than revised/2nd edition etc<br /> <br /> I would just modify the numbers a little bit(keeping in mind that the paradigm of high ranking techncorats is not exactly the same as their subordinate),but the overall idea is superb. The good thing with it is that it would work greatly with say, a homebrew that combines the Arete system with the Pillars<br /> So thumbs up from me<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:41:59-07:00","id":1388145,"title":"","content":"Well, it seems like the OP is stuck in a paradox between the problem of discarding instruments and being set on a specific number of instruments being discarded at a certain rate to follow RAW.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver has a straightforward solution of ditching instruments as you increase in Arete--and by tying it to the power of the effects it also makes in-game sense. After all, if sensing stuff is easy, you should be able to do it without instruments sooner than a spell which requires much more understanding of the Spheres.<br /> <br /> As for 7 instruments, that number need not be the number. 7 instruments works for the math of starting with a variety of ways to do magic so you aren't just using one or two and giving you an option. 7 Also works for the math if you want to have them all discarded for non-Technomancers to get to 'started ditching at Arete 3 and ditched them all by Arete 10' 7 instruments also keeps the required list to a more manageable side--if someone had 20 different instruments to keep track of, that's a lot more resource management to play the game.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say if you like the stabilization of 7 instruments and discarding starting at Arete 3, if the character has more than 7, you could use Dataweaver's method or you could take the total instruments and parcel out the disposal into 7 sets. If someone had 14 instruments, they'd drop 2 per Arete over 3. If they have 17, well you'd go with some odd and even numbers.<br /> <br /> Unless you're playing an official game at an organized play event or playing with a group that requires RAW, you can house rule all you want. You've got a lot of reasons and a good rationale to make some rules tweaks if it makes the game more fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:59:20-07:00","id":1388149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388123-help-me-understand-discarding-instruments-in-m20?p=1388145#post1388145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it seems like the OP is stuck in a paradox between the problem of discarding instruments and being set on a specific number of instruments being discarded at a certain rate to follow RAW.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver has a straightforward solution of ditching instruments as you increase in Arete--and by tying it to the power of the effects it also makes in-game sense. After all, if sensing stuff is easy, you should be able to do it without instruments sooner than a spell which requires much more understanding of the Spheres.<br /> <br /> As for 7 instruments, that number need not be the number. 7 instruments works for the math of starting with a variety of ways to do magic so you aren't just using one or two and giving you an option. 7 Also works for the math if you want to have them all discarded for non-Technomancers to get to 'started ditching at Arete 3 and ditched them all by Arete 10' 7 instruments also keeps the required list to a more manageable side--if someone had 20 different instruments to keep track of, that's a lot more resource management to play the game.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say if you like the stabilization of 7 instruments and discarding starting at Arete 3, if the character has more than 7, you could use Dataweaver's method or you could take the total instruments and parcel out the disposal into 7 sets. If someone had 14 instruments, they'd drop 2 per Arete over 3. If they have 17, well you'd go with some odd and even numbers.<br /> <br /> Unless you're playing an official game at an organized play event or playing with a group that requires RAW, you can house rule all you want. You've got a lot of reasons and a good rationale to make some rules tweaks if it makes the game more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, dropping 2 per arete could work, this is what i actually suggested in my edit above*., but you are left with the arduous task of thinking &quot;would x effect be castable using y instrument that i just internalized? For every single spell. Without even taking into account the fact that the very same mage could do the same effect in a plethora of different ways. Not unlike many real life sciences<br /> <br /> I think that dataweaver's explanation makes a lot more sense conceptually. In-game i always found it funny when a mage gained an Arete point and then said&quot; uhm, ok Forces i choose you&quot;. I could think of in-game explanations but it always seemed a bit too crude and &quot;flat to me<br /> <br /> * but keep in mind that this is not what the official rules say. They actually say &quot;One point per Arete&quot;. It's what 's written.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T16:15:26-07:00","id":1388178,"title":"","content":"On BoS, if you use more than 7 Instruments at Arete 6+ you start discarding 2 or more instruments at the time, the general rule is that with Arete 8 you'll have only one instrument left, you start discarding by the instrument you use LEAST and by Arete 8 you'll have only your principal instrument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T16:30:31-07:00","id":1388179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GothicxXx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388123-help-me-understand-discarding-instruments-in-m20?p=1388178#post1388178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On BoS, if you use more than 7 Instruments at Arete 6+ you start discarding 2 or more instruments at the time, the general rule is that with Arete 8 you'll have only one instrument left, you start discarding by the instrument you use LEAST and by Arete 8 you'll have only your principal instrument.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually found it myself! Yeah it makes much more sense now. The system is still more complicated than the old one, but that may not be a bad thing by its self. Would be great if the old discarding system had been mentioned as optional though(For new players without access to the old books)<br /> <br /> Although the book doesn't mention it, i think it makes perfect sense to extend this even further. E.g for paradigms who have a LOT of instruments you might discard 2 at each point of Arete at 3-5 then 3 later on or possibly even more. (ok, granted this would raise some eyebrows for most characters, but it's just a hypothetical example of how you could logically extrapolate the system)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T19:04:28-07:00","id":1388206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388123-help-me-understand-discarding-instruments-in-m20?p=1388179#post1388179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually found it myself! Yeah it makes much more sense now. The system is still more complicated than the old one, but that may not be a bad thing by its self. Would be great if the old discarding system had been mentioned as optional though(For new players without access to the old books)</div> </div> </div> </div>For me is actually a lot better than bound Instruments into Spheres like the old system was, a character with lots of Instruments would be versatile but still it's a huge drawback in my opinion, if you try to stick to the 7 or trying to limit at 10 would be better, because you also need the Abilities to keep up with the Pratice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T00:02:46-07:00","id":1388252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GothicxXx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388123-help-me-understand-discarding-instruments-in-m20?p=1388206#post1388206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me is actually a lot better than bound Instruments into Spheres like the old system was,</div> </div> </div> </div>This so very much. It never made sense to me to have a specific instrument tied to a specific sphere, given that a single Sphere's effects can do very very different things - things that, at least in my headspace, would require many practices to perform very different acts to get them done.<br /> <br /> As an example, Time. You can scry the future with it! So oracular! Let's say that a good (dare one say greek) instrument for that is kneeling over a gap in the ground and inhaling strange fumes. Strange fumes! Good instrument to tie to that sphere, right?<br /> <br /> ...eeexcept in the old system those fumes also now get used to speed you up, slow you down, count time down to the nanosecond, trap people in an area in a time bubble, hang spells and replace a TARDIS.<br /> Yeah, I like the new system's detachment from the spheres a lot better.<br /> <br /> Heck, the concept of specific spheres being tied to specific instruments per character kind of ran contrary to the very concept of rotes being shared within a Tradition..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-14-2020, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T00:15:39-07:00","id":1388256,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, there's still a lingering remnant of that system in M20, in terms of (I think) unique Instruments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T00:30:56-07:00","id":1388258,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Yeah, nevermind, those are still tied to a sphere - which is kind of silly. Personalized Instruments are, too.<br /> <br /> A good solution would be to make Personalized Instruments a very very specific thing that replaces a general instrument. Say, instead of 'wands' you get 'wands carved frome ebonwood, engraved with silver that was blessed under moonlight for three days'.<br /> If instead of putting a rather general type of instrument down on your character you put down something very individual, you get that -1. No sphere tie-in needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-14-2020, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T03:14:01-07:00","id":1388282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388123-help-me-understand-discarding-instruments-in-m20?p=1388252#post1388252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This so very much. It never made sense to me to have a specific instrument tied to a specific sphere, given that a single Sphere's effects can do very very different things - things that, at least in my headspace, would require many practices to perform very different acts to get them done.<br /> <br /> As an example, Time. You can scry the future with it! So oracular! Let's say that a good (dare one say greek) instrument for that is kneeling over a gap in the ground and inhaling strange fumes. Strange fumes! Good instrument to tie to that sphere, right?<br /> <br /> ...eeexcept in the old system those fumes also now get used to speed you up, slow you down, count time down to the nanosecond, trap people in an area in a time bubble, hang spells and replace a TARDIS.<br /> Yeah, I like the new system's detachment from the spheres a lot better.<br /> <br /> Heck, the concept of specific spheres being tied to specific instruments per character kind of ran contrary to the very concept of rotes being shared within a Tradition..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't that rule ignored by everyone though? For a definition of everyone that includes&quot; The writers that rote the tradition books and all the rotes in every single book ever published&quot;*<br /> <br /> Detaching specific instruments from spheres was definitely a good idea... i am just worried that the current system went too far in the opposite direction. After all not every beginning player can know that ,for example, having only 7 instruments for a Wu Lung is not a Wu lung but rather a Chinese Harry Potter Wizard.<br /> Of course i would not dream of forcing someone to play a character that they do not want too, rather my issue is that the player himself will end up not enjoying his character, precisely because he unintentionally took away all the flavor that makes this game &quot;deeper&quot; than Dungeons and dragons<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So while i don't like the &quot;official&quot; revised system, i do like the one that was de facto used which basically said &quot; You are a wu lung, your foci are the foci of Chinese high-ritualism plus/minus what makes sense for character flavor<br /> <br /> For example, Lee Ann Milner, the signature ecstatic character does not use drugs..because she is traumatized by them. Some Hermetics (such as Criamon) use tattoos.. or sex(Aleister Crowley) or blood or Techno-mysticism(i.e all Thig members), some Akashics/wu lung may have found a little more common ground with each other than they would like to admit. But the core of the paradigm does remain. There is no such thing as an Akashic without meditation/Martial arts, a Hermetic without Symbols(among a shitload of other things), a Chorister without prayers and according to a US Supreme court ruling dating back to 1998 <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">if a players wants to play a solificati without Alchemy, i reserve the right to shoot him in the face and call it self defense<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <br /> *<br /> And i do believe that the(never followed anyway), rule about tying foci to spheres was explicitly dropped at later books..it's just that in typical white wolf fashion a rule can be outright retconned for 20 books, but it will take 2+ iteration of core rulebooks before it's actually changed in the main book itsself<br /> <br /> For example, i think it was in Dark ages mage that this rule was done away with explicitly<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}